**Implementation** (commit `74496f2`):
- `server/config.ts` — `TRANSCRIPT_MERGE_MAX_S: z.coerce.number().nonnegative().default(10)`, documented block in `.env.example`
- `server/session/srt.ts` — new `extendCue` (extends end timestamp + appends to source line, preserves translation line) and `setCueTranslation` (appends or replaces the last text line), both on the `insertTranslationLine` block-scan pattern
- `server/session/writer.ts` — `SessionWriterOptions`, 4th `create` param, `lastCue`/`cueOfIndex`/`mergedCues`/`cueTranslations` bookkeeping. Merge rule: `seg.speaker === lastCue.speaker && seg.end_s - lastCue.start_s < mergeMaxS` (strict `<`, no gap constraint, speaker-less merges with speaker-less). `appendTranslation` routes merged indices to the surviving cue and rewrites the line with all contributing translations joined in index order; non-merged path unchanged
- `server/session/manager.ts` — passes `{ mergeMaxS: config.TRANSCRIPT_MERGE_MAX_S }` to `SessionWriter.create`

**Tests**: new describes for `extendCue`/`setCueTranslation` in `srt.test.ts`, a 7-test merge describe in `writer.test.ts` (threshold, speaker switch with numbering gap, speaker-less, chain merge, disabled byte-identical, both translation orderings, `index+1` binding), config parse/reject tests, and an e2e in `app.test.ts` with a second instance at `TRANSCRIPT_MERGE_MAX_S=5` asserting one merged cue `Speaker 1: Hello. there.` / `XIN CHÀO XIN CHÀO`. Shared e2e env pinned to `'0'` per the plan.

